; reversing then mapping = mapping then reversing: rev(map L) = map(rev L)
; map = elementwise increment, rev = list reversal. By list induction: nil trivial; cons via rev-cons + map-append (map distributes over append) + the IH. A list-program-correctness theorem (map/rev commute) -- the kind Omega's verifier discharges.
